      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5af396c4af8a7e5f9cf76989|full_name}: As a person who has Epilepsy I'm going to have to concur with this.  As you said it is up to the person who has seizures to control their exposure to the things that can cause them. The only responsibility the company has is to put a warning for users that content within VRChat may cause seizures and even that is being nice since the content that may cause one isn't being directly created by them.\n\nAny further policing tools put in place by the company would just lead to abuse by users. It would not even need to be more than one or two out of a hundred users to create a large and negative impact by a mechanism that was intended to help people, when really the people with the seizures need to be not playing the game or accepting the risks that come along with it playing it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
